From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 05:12:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] combase: Implement RoGetParameterizedTypeInstanceIID.

The IID of a Windows Runtime type instance, such as IVector<String>, is
the version 5 (SHA-1) UUID of its signature in the namespace the type
system names; .NET's Windows Runtime support asks for it, and Wine
answered E_NOTIMPL.  As on Windows 11 (tools/paramiidprobe in
wine-altars): the fourteen fundamental types are known by name, case
sensitive, and every other name goes to the caller's locator, in order;
a struct's fields, an enum's base type and a class or group's default
interface by name are types too; the type need not be parameterized.
Missing or extra arguments are E_INVALIDARG, no names or no fields
E_UNEXPECTED, and a locator's error is passed on, with the IID cleared
and the signature so far still handed out.  A locator that describes
nothing is E_UNEXPECTED here, where Windows makes up a type.

RoParameterizedTypeExtraGetTypeSignature and
RoFreeParameterizedTypeExtra give out and free the signature.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

